  data: {
    LLM: "In early rounds, focus on your 4ndcard hand, as it is harder to complete and often represents a larger portion of the pot.\n\nWaste management: If you draw a high card (King/Queen) that doesn't fit your runs, keep it as a 'High Card' kicker for a pair rather than letting opponents pick it up from the discard pile.\n\nRound Counting: Since you only have 6 turns, if by turn 4 you have no pairs or runs, pivot immediately to building a high-card flush or a simple high-card hand to salvage one of the sub-pots.",
    Player: "In early rounds, focus on your 4ndcard hand, as it is harder to complete and often represents a larger portion of the pot.\n\nWaste management: If you draw a high card (King/Queen) that doesn't fit your runs, keep it as a 'High Card' kicker for a pair rather than letting opponents pick it up from the discard pile.\n\nRound Counting: Since you only have 6 turns, if by turn 4 you have no pairs or runs, pivot immediately to building a high-card flush or a simple high-card hand to salvage one of the sub-pots.",
